details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two wide, shallow matte ceramic bowls placed on an aged oak table, with one bowl sharp in the foreground and the second bowl softly blurred in the background to show two servings. The composition is a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component is clearly visible without being obscured. Each bowl contains a fluffy bed of warm quinoa and vibrant baby arugula, topped with a tender, pan-seared tilapia fillet displaying a vibrant, spiced, golden-brown crust from the paprika and cumin. Beside the fish, slices of pearly-green avocado, bright orange segments, and crisp, translucent-thin radish slices are arranged to show off their distinct colors and textures. A light drizzle of lime-olive oil dressing glistens on the surfaces. A wooden spoon rests casually on the table next to the foreground bowl, and a few scattered quinoa grains and a stray radish slice lie on the oak surface. The lighting is soft natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle, realistic shadows. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small oil droplet on the bowl rim, slightly uneven browning on the fish. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a crumb trail on the surface, a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
